<!--
  Key bindings exposed in the game Settings > Keybindings list under a GearMenu category.

  Bindings.xml is picked up by the client from the addon root automatically - it is NOT
  listed in the .toc. Every binding is a CLICK action on one of the hidden, always-present
  SecureActionButtonTemplate proxy buttons that gui/KeyBindProxy.lua creates at login -
  one per possible gearSlot (MAX_GEAR_BARS x MAX_GEAR_BAR_SLOTS) - and keeps pointed at
  the "/use <slotId>" macro of the gearSlot configured at (bar bindIndex, slot position).
  The real gearSlot frames carry a random gearBar id in their name and can never be
  declared here, which is why the proxies exist.

  The PREFACE_ entries render as a text row per gearBar. The names of the actions and the
  rows come from the BINDING_HEADER_GEARMENU / PREFACE_GEARMENU_BAR<b> / BINDING_NAME_
  globals gui/KeyBindProxy.lua sets from the localization at load time. The button names
  must match RGGM_CONSTANTS.ELEMENT_KEY_BIND_PROXY_NAME and the bar / slot bounds
  RGGM_CONSTANTS.MAX_GEAR_BARS / MAX_GEAR_BAR_SLOTS in code/Constants.lua.
-->
